<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alhambra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Alhambra is a palace and fortress complex on the Sabika hill above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. Begun by the Nasrid founder Muhammad I in the 13th century, its finest palaces, including the Court of the Lions, were built under Yusuf I and Muhammad V in the 14th century, decorated with carved stucco, tilework and poems on its walls. It is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alhambra.jpg" alt="Alhambra" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jebulon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dawn_Charles_V_Palace_Alhambra_Granada_Andalusia_Spain.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
